WEBVTT

00:00:14.570 --> 00:00:16.160
Polar Bear's Café

00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:20.450
Polar Bear's Café

00:01:29.980 --> 00:01:34.990
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:01:31.820 --> 00:01:34.260
Mr. Handa's Discussion!

00:01:39.230 --> 00:01:40.870
Polar Bear.

00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:44.020
Thanks for meeting with me today.

00:01:44.470 --> 00:01:47.400
The café is slow today due to 
the rain, so it's no problem.

00:01:48.080 --> 00:01:49.220
I wanted to discuss—

00:01:49.220 --> 00:01:52.040
Hello, Mr. Polar Bear, Mr. Handa.

00:01:55.700 --> 00:01:58.340
Let me know whenever 
you're ready to order.

00:02:04.130 --> 00:02:08.420
And so, I wanted to discuss...

00:02:16.110 --> 00:02:18.820
What are you making, Miss Sasako?

00:02:18.820 --> 00:02:21.110
It's a prototype for a new cake.

00:02:21.110 --> 00:02:22.450
A roll cake?

00:02:23.980 --> 00:02:26.310
It's no ordinary roll cake.

00:02:29.330 --> 00:02:31.540
It's a panda roll cake!

00:02:34.950 --> 00:02:38.680
Panda-shaped foods are so enticing.

00:02:39.520 --> 00:02:41.520
They're cute to begin with,

00:02:41.520 --> 00:02:44.260
but then the inside of your 
mouth becomes cute, too.

00:02:44.970 --> 00:02:47.070
What am I to do?

00:02:47.070 --> 00:02:49.270
Wow. That's rough.

00:02:50.180 --> 00:02:52.250
I'm going to let it cool in the fridge,

00:02:52.250 --> 00:02:53.770
but let's try it later.

00:02:54.130 --> 00:02:55.980
Yay! I'm excited.

00:02:56.500 --> 00:02:59.520
Oh, could I get another 
café mocha, Miss Sasako?

00:02:59.520 --> 00:03:00.210
Sure.

00:03:04.040 --> 00:03:05.590
Mr. Penguin.

00:03:05.590 --> 00:03:06.660
What's up?

00:03:07.220 --> 00:03:10.300
There aren't many customers 
today because of the rain.

00:03:10.300 --> 00:03:12.930
Mr. Handa could have 
talked to Miss Sasako

00:03:12.930 --> 00:03:14.600
a lot if he were here.

00:03:14.600 --> 00:03:15.630
Good point.

00:03:16.140 --> 00:03:18.190
He has terrible luck, as usual.

00:03:19.250 --> 00:03:21.900
The zoo is closed today,

00:03:21.900 --> 00:03:23.970
so I wonder why he isn't here.

00:03:24.670 --> 00:03:25.600
Who knows?

00:03:30.650 --> 00:03:33.950
I'll ask her a whole bunch 
of questions for him.

00:03:34.680 --> 00:03:38.140
You just can't stay still, can you?

00:03:39.410 --> 00:03:40.990
There you go.

00:03:41.940 --> 00:03:45.430
Miss Sasako, you're 
bright and charming

00:03:45.430 --> 00:03:48.570
so you're probably really 
popular with zookeepers.

00:03:49.060 --> 00:03:50.450
That's too direct!

00:03:52.320 --> 00:03:55.320
Oh, Panda, stop it!

00:03:57.120 --> 00:03:59.920
I'm tall and I have broad shoulders,

00:03:59.920 --> 00:04:02.330
so I'm always told I'm not feminine.

00:04:02.330 --> 00:04:04.500
If you know someone, 
I'd like you to introduce him.

00:04:04.500 --> 00:04:05.230
What?

00:04:06.000 --> 00:04:08.500
Well, how broad are your shoulders?

00:04:09.520 --> 00:04:13.010
U-Um, what kind of guys do 
you like, Miss Sasako?

00:04:13.010 --> 00:04:13.520
Huh?

00:04:14.600 --> 00:04:18.230
Someone who's taller than 
me and comforting.

00:04:18.230 --> 00:04:19.330
What?!

00:04:21.010 --> 00:04:22.330
Welcome!

00:04:23.280 --> 00:04:25.820
W-What are we going to do?

00:04:28.460 --> 00:04:30.500
I've come by again today, Miss Sasako,

00:04:31.780 --> 00:04:35.710
since I look forward to having 
great coffee here on my days off.

00:04:35.710 --> 00:04:36.980
Well, thank you very much.

00:04:38.520 --> 00:04:42.510
Could I get another 
coffee, Miss Sasako?

00:04:42.990 --> 00:04:44.250
Coming right up.

00:04:46.080 --> 00:04:49.460
What's the lunch special 
today, Miss Sasako?

00:04:50.360 --> 00:04:53.640
Our main dish today is
savory fried soy meat.

00:04:56.000 --> 00:04:59.080
Aren't there a lot of 
good looking customers?

00:04:59.080 --> 00:05:01.200
Mr. Handa's in trouble.

00:05:03.490 --> 00:05:05.240
And so, I wanted to discuss...

00:05:05.240 --> 00:05:06.130
Yes?

00:05:09.140 --> 00:05:12.080
Is Miss Sasako dating anyone?

00:05:14.550 --> 00:05:16.040
Actually...

00:05:16.490 --> 00:05:17.410
Actually?!

00:05:18.270 --> 00:05:21.500
I haven't had lunch yet. 
Mind if I eat something?

00:05:23.080 --> 00:05:24.970
Sure! It'll be on me!

00:05:24.970 --> 00:05:34.930
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:05:35.560 --> 00:05:39.540
I'll have one of the deluxe lunches 
you only make five of per day.

00:05:39.540 --> 00:05:41.580
You're getting the most 
expensive thing?!

00:05:43.500 --> 00:05:45.660
U-Uh, go ahead...

00:05:46.140 --> 00:05:48.990
One deluxe lunch coming right up.

00:05:52.550 --> 00:05:53.950
Actually...

00:05:55.350 --> 00:05:56.660
Actually?!

00:05:57.280 --> 00:06:00.420
I wanted to order the soup set, too.

00:06:02.430 --> 00:06:05.130
Could we add on a soup set, Lesser?

00:06:05.630 --> 00:06:09.590
It looks like Miss Sasako doesn't 
have a boyfriend right now.

00:06:11.490 --> 00:06:13.600
I-I see.

00:06:16.080 --> 00:06:17.270
But...

00:06:17.560 --> 00:06:18.500
But?!

00:06:19.320 --> 00:06:22.670
I heard she prefers someone
tall and comforting.

00:06:25.590 --> 00:06:28.950
I think I'm at least five centimeters 
shorter than Miss Sasako...

00:06:30.240 --> 00:06:31.450
Not to worry.

00:06:31.940 --> 00:06:33.820
Just wear these elevator boots.

00:06:34.500 --> 00:06:36.910
It'd be strange if I grew 
suddenly, wouldn't it?

00:06:37.390 --> 00:06:38.310
Then...

00:06:39.540 --> 00:06:41.720
shall we make Miss Sasako shorter?

00:06:42.240 --> 00:06:44.730
Are you taking this 
seriously, Polar Bear?

00:06:47.040 --> 00:06:48.720
Thank you for waiting.

00:06:53.000 --> 00:06:55.320
Well, I don't think you'll have to

00:06:55.320 --> 00:06:57.220
worry much about her preferences.

00:06:58.370 --> 00:06:59.180
Really?

00:06:59.790 --> 00:07:03.060
For example, I prefer seals.

00:07:03.820 --> 00:07:07.150
But if I can't catch any seals, 
I'll eat walruses, too.

00:07:07.520 --> 00:07:10.580
Don't compare this with 
your food preferences!

00:07:10.580 --> 00:07:14.660
It's not like I wanted to be 
born shaped like a walrus.

00:07:14.660 --> 00:07:15.500
Oh?

00:07:16.780 --> 00:07:18.830
Walrus <i>(Seiuchi)</i>?

00:07:19.540 --> 00:07:20.710
Right about here.

00:07:20.710 --> 00:07:22.040
That would be the 
Seto region <i>(Seto Uchi)</i>.

00:07:23.520 --> 00:07:24.890
That would be a 
log cabin <i>(ki no uchi)</i>.

00:07:25.420 --> 00:07:26.340
Ow!

00:07:27.120 --> 00:07:28.850
That would be a surprise 
attack <i>(fuiuchi)</i>.

00:07:29.810 --> 00:07:31.480
And this would be striking 
simultaneously <i>(aiuchi)</i>.

00:07:32.580 --> 00:07:35.180
This is really poor behavior towards
someone who's really troubled <i>(shiuchi)</i>.

00:07:35.180 --> 00:07:38.810
This is a 
couch <i>(kauchi)</i>.

00:07:35.940 --> 00:07:37.510
Well played.

00:07:38.810 --> 00:07:41.310
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:07:42.000 --> 00:07:46.770
Well, I'll help you think of 
a way to get closer to her.

00:07:46.990 --> 00:07:48.400
Really?

00:07:48.400 --> 00:07:50.550
I'll feel more confident after getting advice

00:07:50.550 --> 00:07:52.740
from you since you're so popular.

00:07:53.910 --> 00:07:55.700
I think...

00:07:56.260 --> 00:07:57.660
You think?

00:08:00.390 --> 00:08:03.600
...that the desserts here 
are delicious, too.

00:08:03.600 --> 00:08:05.570
B-Be my guest!

00:08:05.570 --> 00:08:07.910
Order whatever you'd like!

00:08:10.240 --> 00:08:11.840
How was the lunch special?

00:08:11.840 --> 00:08:14.460
It was healthy and the 
flavor was great.

00:08:14.460 --> 00:08:16.250
Thank you very much.

00:08:16.250 --> 00:08:19.020
Oh, could I get a lemon tea, too?

00:08:16.250 --> 00:08:19.880
Miss Sasako's getting even friendlier 
with the handsome guy.

00:08:19.020 --> 00:08:20.410
Certainly. Coming right up.

00:08:19.880 --> 00:08:21.510
Dang it!

00:08:33.260 --> 00:08:34.390
A text?

00:08:34.900 --> 00:08:35.970
I wonder who it's from.

00:08:37.470 --> 00:08:39.450
Oh, it's from Mr. Llama.

00:08:39.840 --> 00:08:41.710
<i>If you ask me,</i>

00:08:41.710 --> 00:08:44.110
<i>continuing to admire her from afar</i>

00:08:44.110 --> 00:08:47.320
<i>isn't out of the question, either.</i>

00:08:49.590 --> 00:08:51.380
What's with this picture message?

00:08:52.190 --> 00:08:56.120
I sent out a text to everyone 
asking for any advice.

00:08:56.120 --> 00:08:57.230
What?!

00:08:57.840 --> 00:08:59.220
E-Everyone?

00:08:59.660 --> 00:09:00.750
Everyone.

00:09:02.230 --> 00:09:04.020
<i>Nothing can beat cleanliness</i>

00:09:04.020 --> 00:09:06.340
<i>and a heartfelt regard for others.</i>

00:09:06.340 --> 00:09:08.520
<i>Mr. Handa, good luck!</i>

00:09:09.520 --> 00:09:10.960
Lesser?

00:09:16.820 --> 00:09:19.050
<i>You have terrible luck, Mr. Handa,</i>

00:09:19.050 --> 00:09:21.300
<i>so you need to try to 
use that in your favor.</i>

00:09:21.300 --> 00:09:23.570
What do you mean, 
"use that in my favor"?

00:09:25.020 --> 00:09:27.240
<i>Mr. Handa, you idiot!</i>

00:09:31.460 --> 00:09:32.860
What is this?!

00:09:32.860 --> 00:09:35.020
And what does he mean by "idiot"?

00:09:36.050 --> 00:09:38.390
From:    Miss Sasako

00:09:40.180 --> 00:09:41.640
From Miss Sasako, too?!

00:09:42.890 --> 00:09:46.290
<i>I recommend the fried soy meat.</i>

00:09:48.070 --> 00:09:49.300
Good thing

00:09:50.050 --> 00:09:52.990
I asked her for a 
recommendation for lunch.

00:09:51.320 --> 00:09:56.780
Please suggest 
something for lunch 
for Mr. Handa.

00:09:54.840 --> 00:09:56.440
What does that even mean?!

00:09:59.940 --> 00:10:03.040
Jeez, I even sent him a text.

00:10:03.450 --> 00:10:05.590
Mr. Handa's still not here.

00:10:05.590 --> 00:10:08.390
If he doesn't hurry up, 
Miss Sasako's going to be taken.

00:10:10.600 --> 00:10:12.000
Panda!

00:10:18.390 --> 00:10:19.690
M-Miss Sasako!

00:10:19.690 --> 00:10:20.800
The roll cake!

00:10:20.800 --> 00:10:23.470
I'd like to eat the roll 
cake right about now!

00:10:23.470 --> 00:10:25.040
Oh, really?

00:10:25.040 --> 00:10:25.930
Would you like some now?

00:10:25.930 --> 00:10:32.940
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:10:33.660 --> 00:10:34.890
Here you go.

00:10:36.200 --> 00:10:37.700
Oh my, Panda...

00:10:39.640 --> 00:10:41.420
Please don't glare like that.

00:10:41.420 --> 00:10:43.300
Were you waiting that long?

00:10:43.830 --> 00:10:45.660
<i>Mr. Handa...</i>

00:10:46.040 --> 00:10:47.660
<i>You idiot!</i>

00:10:53.470 --> 00:10:55.740
It's angry!

00:10:55.740 --> 00:10:57.080
A cardinal mistake!

00:10:57.080 --> 00:10:58.510
Is it because of Panda?

00:11:00.420 --> 00:11:00.970
Huh?

00:11:04.430 --> 00:11:06.920
It looks so stern! How cool!

00:11:06.920 --> 00:11:07.990
Huh?!

00:11:10.450 --> 00:11:11.350
Mr. Handa.

00:11:13.080 --> 00:11:16.030
I think you should stay 
just the way you are.

00:11:17.790 --> 00:11:18.990
Because

00:11:19.740 --> 00:11:22.950
that's what's great about you.

00:11:27.090 --> 00:11:28.220
Thank you.

00:11:28.960 --> 00:11:31.410
Come by the café again.

00:11:31.410 --> 00:11:32.980
I'll treat you.

00:11:33.990 --> 00:11:35.000
Sure.

00:11:42.010 --> 00:11:46.930
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:11:43.500 --> 00:11:46.260
Panda Mama's Daily Life.

00:11:51.410 --> 00:11:53.450
<i>Hello, everyone.</i>

00:11:53.450 --> 00:11:55.070
<i>My name is Panda Mama.</i>

00:11:55.560 --> 00:11:57.090
<i>I'm out buying groceries</i>

00:11:57.090 --> 00:11:59.310
<i>at the supermarket for my family.</i>

00:12:01.000 --> 00:12:03.770
I think we'll have a 
combination platter of

00:12:03.770 --> 00:12:05.680
bamboo and bamboo grass again tonight.

00:12:08.240 --> 00:12:09.410
Advertised 
Item!

00:12:08.240 --> 00:12:09.410
Walnuts

00:12:08.240 --> 00:12:09.410
All you 
can stuff!

00:12:10.580 --> 00:12:12.670
All you can stuff walnuts!

00:12:13.320 --> 00:12:16.040
Everyone loves them so I'll get some.

00:12:22.070 --> 00:12:23.910
This looks good.

00:12:23.910 --> 00:12:25.500
I got quite a few in.

00:12:25.500 --> 00:12:27.970
Oh, if it isn't Panda Mama.

00:12:28.840 --> 00:12:31.850
Well, hello, Mama Red Squirrel.

00:12:31.850 --> 00:12:35.270
Well if it isn't all you 
can stuff walnuts!

00:12:35.900 --> 00:12:38.770
Walnuts are our favorite!

00:12:39.220 --> 00:12:41.460
My family loves them, too.

00:12:42.040 --> 00:12:46.480
Goodness, what's with this stuffing? 
There's no enthusiasm.

00:12:46.480 --> 00:12:48.780
Really? I got quite a few in there.

00:12:50.880 --> 00:12:53.770
That wouldn't be considered 
all you can stuff!

00:12:54.540 --> 00:12:57.110
You're too gentle, Panda Mama.

00:12:57.110 --> 00:13:00.590
You won't be able to survive in
 this capitalist society like that!

00:13:01.390 --> 00:13:04.170
Then what should I do?

00:13:04.170 --> 00:13:06.680
When you're dealing with 
all you can stuff,

00:13:07.580 --> 00:13:10.640
you have to stretch out the bag first.

00:13:10.910 --> 00:13:13.510
Oh, I didn't know that.

00:13:13.510 --> 00:13:15.200
You stretch it out as 
far as it'll go,

00:13:15.200 --> 00:13:17.630
just before it's about to rip.

00:13:17.630 --> 00:13:19.420
There's no point if it rips,

00:13:19.420 --> 00:13:21.490
so being extra careful is crucial.

00:13:24.960 --> 00:13:27.450
That looks about good.

00:13:28.430 --> 00:13:30.580
Now let's start stuffing.

00:13:30.580 --> 00:13:31.700
Okay.

00:13:33.510 --> 00:13:35.370
No, no, you're doing it wrong.

00:13:35.890 --> 00:13:38.140
You can't fill it so carelessly.

00:13:38.140 --> 00:13:38.880
What?

00:13:39.060 --> 00:13:40.410
Listen.

00:13:40.410 --> 00:13:42.580
You start from the edges!

00:13:43.400 --> 00:13:45.370
E-Edges?

00:13:45.370 --> 00:13:48.310
You carefully measure it out 
so you don't leave any gaps.

00:13:48.310 --> 00:13:49.790
O-Okay.

00:13:50.910 --> 00:13:52.570
When you're dealing with 
all you can stuff,

00:13:52.570 --> 00:13:55.560
you feel special the 
more you can stuff.

00:13:55.560 --> 00:13:57.980
Then you can seek out even 
better methods of stuffing.

00:13:59.080 --> 00:14:01.910
It's a true form of 
shopping entertainment!

00:14:03.160 --> 00:14:05.400
Oh my! I had no idea.

00:14:05.400 --> 00:14:10.410
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:14:14.110 --> 00:14:16.430
I got quite a bit in there.

00:14:17.040 --> 00:14:19.620
Oh, Mama Red Squirrel.

00:14:19.620 --> 00:14:22.040
Looks like you have 
a slight gap there.

00:14:23.340 --> 00:14:24.560
Oh, you're right!

00:14:24.560 --> 00:14:27.220
I was completely off guard.

00:14:29.170 --> 00:14:32.510
Looks like you're starting to 
get it, as well, Panda Mama.

00:14:33.330 --> 00:14:35.690
But it's filled to the brim.

00:14:35.690 --> 00:14:37.140
I don't think we can fit any more.

00:14:37.140 --> 00:14:39.130
What are you talking about?

00:14:39.130 --> 00:14:41.360
The battle starts here!

00:14:56.120 --> 00:14:58.410
I'm so sorry, Mama Red Squirrel!

00:14:58.410 --> 00:15:01.330
I shouldn't have said anything.

00:15:03.790 --> 00:15:05.480
I let down my guard.

00:15:05.480 --> 00:15:07.080
I was too arrogant.

00:15:09.500 --> 00:15:12.560
Let's stuff another bag 
together, Mama Red Squirrel.

00:15:13.110 --> 00:15:16.300
I'm sorry I said you
 were too gentle earlier.

00:15:16.300 --> 00:15:17.500
Don't say that.

00:15:17.500 --> 00:15:19.950
I learned a valuable lesson.

00:15:20.920 --> 00:15:22.980
By the way, Mama Red Squirrel,

00:15:22.980 --> 00:15:25.410
want to go to an all-you-can-eat 
cake buffet afterwards?

00:15:25.410 --> 00:15:27.980
I promised Ms. King Penguin 
I'd meet up with her.

00:15:27.980 --> 00:15:29.950
Oh, sounds wonderful!

00:15:31.420 --> 00:15:33.690
Thanks for everything!

00:15:32.600 --> 00:15:33.690
See you later.

00:15:35.830 --> 00:15:39.080
Panda Mama didn't know a thing.

00:15:39.080 --> 00:15:41.290
Oh, really?

00:15:41.720 --> 00:15:44.630
Well, you can call the 
all-you-can-eat cake buffet

00:15:44.630 --> 00:15:46.080
the entertainment of sweets,

00:15:46.080 --> 00:15:47.400
since you can enjoy both the

00:15:47.400 --> 00:15:51.260
fun of contemplating and the 
deliciousness of eating.

00:15:52.990 --> 00:15:54.180
Oh, my!

00:16:00.930 --> 00:16:03.350
Everything looks so delicious!

00:16:04.250 --> 00:16:05.730
Pe-pen!

00:16:06.500 --> 00:16:08.350
Not so fast, Panda Mama!

00:16:08.700 --> 00:16:09.570
What?

00:16:10.160 --> 00:16:12.380
Once you've scoped out the lineup,

00:16:12.380 --> 00:16:14.050
you have to rank them.

00:16:14.050 --> 00:16:15.790
The ones you definitely want to eat.

00:16:14.070 --> 00:16:20.200
Definitely want 
to eat

00:16:15.790 --> 00:16:18.170
Then the ones you want 
to eat after that.

00:16:16.080 --> 00:16:20.200
Runner-ups

00:16:17.910 --> 00:16:20.200
If there's any room left

00:16:18.170 --> 00:16:20.200
Only then, can you put 
things on your plate.

00:16:20.460 --> 00:16:23.200
I see. I understand now.

00:16:25.040 --> 00:16:27.010
The one I want to eat the most

00:16:27.010 --> 00:16:28.710
is the strawberry shortcake.

00:16:29.720 --> 00:16:31.300
Pe-pen!

00:16:32.560 --> 00:16:35.140
The standard of an 
all-you-can-eat buffet is

00:16:35.140 --> 00:16:36.890
to eat your second favorite first.

00:16:37.220 --> 00:16:38.670
That's a standard?

00:16:38.670 --> 00:16:41.700
If you eat your favorite first, you'll rush

00:16:41.700 --> 00:16:43.570
and you won't enjoy the flavor.

00:16:43.570 --> 00:16:46.400
There's no point in eating your 
favorite if you can't enjoy it.

00:16:46.400 --> 00:16:48.570
Precisely, Mama Red Squirrel.

00:16:48.940 --> 00:16:51.600
The all-you-can-eat cake buffet 
tests your way of living.

00:16:52.310 --> 00:16:55.200
It's a hard-boiled battlefield!

00:16:56.170 --> 00:16:58.530
B-Battlefield?

00:16:59.930 --> 00:17:02.390
Now we'll place the 
cake on our plates.

00:17:02.950 --> 00:17:05.910
The thing to remember here is 
not to overfill your plate.

00:17:05.910 --> 00:17:07.940
Just grab three or four.

00:17:07.940 --> 00:17:10.590
What? That's it?

00:17:11.140 --> 00:17:12.500
Indeed.

00:17:12.500 --> 00:17:15.550
You use a different plate 
for your second round.

00:17:16.010 --> 00:17:20.010
But wouldn't that make the 
dishwasher's life harder?

00:17:20.010 --> 00:17:21.970
Who cares?!

00:17:24.330 --> 00:17:26.590
A-All right.

00:17:35.920 --> 00:17:38.550
It's a bit of a hassle having 
to go back and forth

00:17:38.550 --> 00:17:41.250
when you fill your 
plate with so little.

00:17:41.250 --> 00:17:43.280
That's what's so great about it.

00:17:43.280 --> 00:17:45.210
If you exercise by getting up 
and sitting back down,

00:17:45.210 --> 00:17:47.580
you'll be able to make room for more.

00:17:47.580 --> 00:17:49.420
You have a point.

00:17:50.300 --> 00:17:53.130
You eat so elegantly, Mama Red Squirrel.

00:17:53.130 --> 00:17:54.710
Well, it's huge.

00:17:54.710 --> 00:17:56.880
If I don't hold it with both 
hands, I can't eat it.

00:17:57.270 --> 00:18:00.010
I guess red squirrels' body size 
puts them at a disadvantage here.

00:18:00.620 --> 00:18:03.180
Why not stuff your cheek pouches?

00:18:04.250 --> 00:18:07.090
Don't group me with chipmunks 
or Japanese monkeys!

00:18:07.090 --> 00:18:09.310
Red squirrels don't have those!

00:18:10.270 --> 00:18:12.550
I-I'm sorry.

00:18:13.070 --> 00:18:14.280
It's fine.

00:18:14.280 --> 00:18:15.570
I'm not angry.

00:18:17.010 --> 00:18:19.930
You eat quite delicately, 
too, Ms. King Penguin.

00:18:20.510 --> 00:18:22.390
There's a trick to it.

00:18:22.390 --> 00:18:23.240
A trick?

00:18:23.760 --> 00:18:26.400
First, you carefully 
hold it in your mouth,

00:18:27.170 --> 00:18:28.870
then bring it up...

00:18:30.330 --> 00:18:31.690
And gulp!

00:18:33.240 --> 00:18:34.190
How's that?

00:18:34.190 --> 00:18:36.890
It's like we can't see 
you eating at all!

00:18:36.890 --> 00:18:39.220
You can gulp down a cake
 like it's a drink.

00:18:41.080 --> 00:18:42.610
Pe-pen!

00:18:43.240 --> 00:18:45.440
What do you mean by "pe-pen"?

00:18:46.090 --> 00:18:48.780
Coffee and tea cost extra!

00:18:48.780 --> 00:18:49.940
Not to mention they're hotel-priced!

00:18:50.770 --> 00:18:52.490
And they charge tax and a service fee!

00:18:52.490 --> 00:18:54.480
Don't drink it unless 
it's an emergency!

00:18:55.120 --> 00:18:57.780
If you're thirsty, just gulp down some cake!

00:19:01.720 --> 00:19:03.980
That's fine and all, but

00:19:03.980 --> 00:19:06.750
my palate is getting 
bored of all the sweets.

00:19:07.540 --> 00:19:09.750
And for that very reason...

00:19:11.000 --> 00:19:14.170
They have light snacks 
ready for you, too.

00:19:14.460 --> 00:19:16.110
I see.

00:19:16.110 --> 00:19:18.220
Since it's an all-you-can-eat 
cake buffet,

00:19:18.220 --> 00:19:20.280
I thought it was just for eating sweets.

00:19:20.930 --> 00:19:23.720
I thought light snacks would be heresy.

00:19:23.720 --> 00:19:25.390
Nonsense.

00:19:25.710 --> 00:19:27.510
Only once you've enjoyed all that an

00:19:27.510 --> 00:19:29.650
all-you-can-eat 
cake buffet has to offer,

00:19:29.650 --> 00:19:31.850
can you be a true all-you-can-eat 
cake buffeter.

00:19:34.030 --> 00:19:37.270
I'm very thankful I came with you two.

00:19:37.270 --> 00:19:39.320
If I had come here alone, I'd—

00:19:39.320 --> 00:19:41.330
Die in battle!

00:19:41.780 --> 00:19:46.790
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:19:50.090 --> 00:19:52.420
I feel so accomplished.

00:19:52.420 --> 00:19:54.210
We did a great job.

00:19:54.600 --> 00:19:56.760
I didn't think you 
were going to be able

00:19:56.760 --> 00:19:59.030
to finish that last plate, Panda Mama.

00:19:59.030 --> 00:20:00.870
I had chills just watching.

00:20:00.870 --> 00:20:03.400
Oh, stop. You're embarrassing me.

00:20:03.890 --> 00:20:06.590
Oh, if it isn't Ms. Tanaka.

00:20:07.420 --> 00:20:10.100
Hello, Panda Mama. 
Are you out running errands?

00:20:10.660 --> 00:20:13.680
Well, you see, Ms. Tanaka, 
listen to this,

00:20:13.680 --> 00:20:15.890
I had a completely productive day.

00:20:15.890 --> 00:20:19.600
My last plate was so full!

00:20:19.600 --> 00:20:20.940
How wonderful.

00:20:20.940 --> 00:20:22.830
Would you care to join 
us for some tea?

00:20:22.830 --> 00:20:24.620
That sounds great. I'd like to rest.

00:20:24.620 --> 00:20:26.640
I'm exhausted from all the eating.

00:20:29.370 --> 00:20:32.990
By the way, my son's a regular here.

00:20:33.460 --> 00:20:36.010
Is your son still working 
the part-time job?

00:20:36.010 --> 00:20:37.340
It appears so.

00:20:37.780 --> 00:20:40.540
He always says hello
 when I see him.

00:20:40.540 --> 00:20:42.690
His courtesies may be 
his only good trait.

00:20:42.690 --> 00:20:44.800
But I'm so worried about his future.

00:20:44.800 --> 00:20:47.200
My son is playing with, 
what are they called, cards?

00:20:47.200 --> 00:20:50.480
He's been playing with them 
so much that I'm worried.

00:20:50.990 --> 00:20:53.020
Seems like everyone's in the same boat.

00:20:53.020 --> 00:20:55.360
Oh, could I get another of the same?

00:20:56.270 --> 00:20:57.000
Yes, ma'am.

00:21:00.900 --> 00:21:02.970
Refills are half price.

00:21:02.970 --> 00:21:04.230
Oh, my!

00:21:04.800 --> 00:21:06.240
It's a service we provide.

00:21:07.320 --> 00:21:10.700
It's a refill and you're 
charging us money?

00:21:11.000 --> 00:21:12.540
It's like a café in a hotel!

00:21:13.020 --> 00:21:15.370
I-I'm terribly sorry.

00:21:15.370 --> 00:21:17.340
Isn't half price a bit expensive?

00:21:17.340 --> 00:21:18.930
We come here every now and then

00:21:18.930 --> 00:21:20.670
so it should be on the house!

00:21:21.140 --> 00:21:22.460
I'm sorry.

00:21:24.680 --> 00:21:27.330
You can't ever let your guard down.

00:21:30.740 --> 00:21:32.890
Oh, where did the time go?

00:21:33.160 --> 00:21:34.980
Oh, you're right.

00:21:36.770 --> 00:21:38.720
Thank you very much!

00:21:38.720 --> 00:21:41.850
Say, let's go to an all-you-can-eat 
lunch buffet next time.

00:21:41.850 --> 00:21:43.750
Sounds great! Where should we go?

00:21:43.750 --> 00:21:45.980
Sounds like you know a good place.

00:21:45.980 --> 00:21:47.240
I do!

00:21:47.240 --> 00:21:50.280
You know the Italian 
restaurant on 1st street, right?

00:21:50.280 --> 00:21:52.640
I've heard great things 
about that place!

00:21:52.640 --> 00:21:53.680
Oh, really?

00:21:53.680 --> 00:21:56.040
We should definitely go there!

00:21:56.040 --> 00:21:58.590
Could I get a refill on my coffee?

00:21:58.590 --> 00:22:01.900
It's a refill of a refill, so it'll 
only be a fourth of the price, right?

00:22:01.900 --> 00:22:04.000
Makes perfect sense to me.

00:22:04.000 --> 00:22:06.710
I'd like a refill, 
too, Mr. Polar Bear.

00:22:06.710 --> 00:22:07.990
Oh, me, too.

00:22:07.990 --> 00:22:10.060
Could I get half price 
on a half price refill?

00:22:10.410 --> 00:22:15.680
Actually, a refill on a refill will 
not make it a lesser price...

00:22:10.660 --> 00:22:12.390
They're not leaving...

00:22:12.390 --> 00:22:14.100
Why are you hiding?

00:22:14.100 --> 00:22:16.730
Or rather, why do I 
have to hide with you?

00:22:15.680 --> 00:22:17.440
What?!

00:22:17.440 --> 00:22:24.940
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:23:54.950 --> 00:24:24.520
Next Time

00:23:58.160 --> 00:23:59.800
Mr. Penguin, Mr. Penguin.

00:23:59.800 --> 00:24:01.080
What is it, Panda?

00:24:01.080 --> 00:24:03.540
Isn't it exciting when we go on trips?

00:24:03.540 --> 00:24:04.310
It is.

00:24:04.310 --> 00:24:06.290
Well since you're so 
excited, why don't you

00:24:06.290 --> 00:24:08.480
throw your life savings out the window?

00:24:08.480 --> 00:24:09.810
The windows won't open,

00:24:09.810 --> 00:24:12.120
not to mention I'm not <i>that</i> excited.

00:24:12.120 --> 00:24:14.660
Then could you shut up for 
a while, Mr. Penguin?

00:24:14.660 --> 00:24:16.000
I'm gonna go to sleep.

00:24:16.000 --> 00:24:17.990
You're the one that started 
talking to me...

00:24:17.990 --> 00:24:19.710
Next week's Polar Bear Café,

00:24:19.710 --> 00:24:21.470
will be presented to 
you in paper craft.

00:24:21.370 --> 00:24:24.000
Panda's Apprenticeship
A Sports Day Filled With Animals

00:24:21.470 --> 00:24:22.610
Let's go with animation.

00:24:22.610 --> 00:24:24.000
Enjoy!
